Scidc - Chess Database
======================

Scidc is a chess database application, forked from Scidb r1531.
It supports reading and writing multiple database formats and includes
built-in chess engine support for game analysis.

Most changes in this fork were developed with the assistance of
Claude (Anthropic AI).

Supported formats
-----------------
- SI5 / SI4 / SI3  (Scid formats, read/write)
- SCI / SCV        (Scidb formats, read/write)
- CBH / CBF        (ChessBase, read only)
- PGN              (import/export)

Requirements
------------
- Linux (x86_64)
- For running: none (AppImage bundles all dependencies)
- For building: gcc/g++, make, Tcl/Tk 8.6 dev headers, X11 dev headers,
  zlib, expat, gdbm

Installation
------------
Scidc is distributed as an AppImage. No installation is required.

Download Scidc-x86_64.AppImage, make it executable and run it:

    chmod +x Scidc-x86_64.AppImage
    ./Scidc-x86_64.AppImage

User data is stored in ~/.scidc-beta/

Building from source
--------------------
See the file INSTALL for detailed build instructions.

